  "result": "I can't fix this yet because I can't tell which `--help` output you mean. I haven't changed anything, since plan mode is on.\n\nThis repo is the Click library itself, not an application with its own CLI. I read the help-generation code and found nothing out of order:\n\n- **Options:** they're listed in the order the decorators are applied, top to bottom. `--help` is always last, because `get_params` appends it (`core.py:1102-1107`). `format_options` (`core.py:1295-1305`) and `write_dl` (`formatting.py:229`) do no sorting.\n- **Arguments:** they get their own \"Arguments\" section, printed before \"Options\".\n- **Subcommands:** they're alphabetical, because `Group.list_commands` returns `sorted(self.commands)` (`core.py:1945`). `CommandCollection.list_commands` sorts too.\n\nNo existing test asserts the order of options or commands in help output.\n\nWhich of these do you mean?\n\n1. **Subcommands:** you want them in registration order rather than alphabetical. The fix would be a small change to `list_commands`, plus a test.\n2. **Options:** you want `--help` listed first, or the options sorted. I'd need to know the order you expect.\n3. **A specific command:** a particular command or example whose output looks wrong. If so, send me the command and the output you see.\n\nTell me which and I'll write up the plan.",
